{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797883-how-intelligent-is-the-horror","id":797883,"title":"How intelligent is the Horror?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-01T11:20:23-08:00","id":797883,"title":"How intelligent is the Horror?","content":"In the corebook, it makes Horrors out to be dumb beasts (small 'b'), basically unthinking bundles of rage and hunger. But what about the ones that, by their nature, have to be clever? The manipulative dragon that talks thieves come to steal its treasure into fighting amongst themselves? The creature that knows all of your darkest secrets and wields them against you as claws and fangs and swords? The monster that you go to to make a deal and always leave with the feeling that you've lost more than you've gained?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T11:44:03-08:00","id":797897,"title":"","content":"Most depictions of Horrors as unthinking bundles of rage are the direct result of, well, starving. They need to be fed, and fed now because, well, they're literally dying of hunger. Can they be clever and silver tongued? Possibly. But here's the question - who's it going to be clever WITH? And is there any reason why you, the Begotten, aren't merged with the Horror when dealing with interuders, considering how easy it is? <br /> <br /> I guess its a case of Schrodinger's Cat. Its both mindless and clever until you actually observe it and find out for sure. If you're observing it, you've merged with it. And then, its all up to your intellect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T12:30:59-08:00","id":797918,"title":"","content":"Well, from what I remember, the Horrors use the 3 ephemeral Attributes, with a minimum determined by the Attributes of the Beast. Power = highest between Strength/Intelligence/Presence, Finesse = highest between Dexterity/Wits/Manipulation and Resistance = highest between Stamina/Resolve/Composure. And then they get a pool of dots equal to Lair x 2 to distribute between those stats and also Size.<br /> <br /> At least on paper, they are just as intelligent as the Beasts, but with a significant boost provided by shedding their human guise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:18:47-08:00","id":797942,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I had thought that maybe they weren't all that clever but they appeared to be because, for the conniving dragon, manipulating people is as much a part of its instincts as biting something is a part of a lion's.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps the Horror itself is mindless;but in place of a mind, the Beast's Id settles in place and takes a hold of the nightmare monster. That would mean that when a Beast tries to communicate with his Horror, he's really just talking to the animalistic side of himself, the side that cares for nothing beyond its own satisfaction. A Horror is just a part of a human. I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-01-2016, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:29:52-08:00","id":797945,"title":"","content":"I just had the funniest thought. imagine what a psychiatrist would think of a Beast:<br /> <br /> Psy.: Well Mr. Smith, what seems to be the problem?<br /> <br /> B.: I have a primordial living nightmare stuck in my head that feeds off of the fear of others.<br /> <br /> Psy.: Errrr....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T21:31:26-08:00","id":798096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797883-how-intelligent-is-the-horror?p=797942#post797942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I had thought that maybe they weren't all that clever but they appeared to be because, for the conniving dragon, manipulating people is as much a part of its instincts as biting something is a part of a lion's.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps the Horror itself is mindless;but in place of a mind, the Beast's Id settles in place and takes a hold of the nightmare monster. That would mean that when a Beast tries to communicate with his Horror, he's really just talking to the animalistic side of himself, the side that cares for nothing beyond its own satisfaction. A Horror is just a part of a human. I like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my take on it as well. It's kind of nonsensical or pointless to think of the Horror and the Begotten as separate creatures; even though they don't use the term anymore, the Horror is the Beast's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:13:02-08:00","id":802297,"title":"","content":"That brings to mind something I read... somewhere a while ago, ahem:<br /> &quot;You do not have a soul. You <i>are</i> a soul. you have a body.&quot;<br /> In this case, the part that the Beast thinks of as 'them' is their conscious mind, while the 'Horror' is really his Id. They're both the Beast, just different parts of the same whole. And that whole is you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T11:01:38-08:00","id":803219,"title":"","content":"The book explicitly compares the Horror to the Beast's Id, if I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-07-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:30:50-08:00","id":803269,"title":"","content":"I remember the comparison but I'm proposing that the Horror not only acts <i>like </i>the Id, it <i>is </i>the Id.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:36:51-08:00","id":803277,"title":"","content":"I think the Horror has always greater Intelligence than the Beast. Power = Intelligence + Lair trait. Unless, the player puts all lair points in Finesse or Resistance. I imagine the Horror as cunning Id that hunts when the Beast sleeps. The stuff that the Horror know the Beast can not even dream about. Literary. And if your Horror has Mirmir's Wisdom, well that's when the fun really starts.<br /> Also, the Beast Incarnate is when the cunning Horror merges the flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:43:32-08:00","id":803281,"title":"","content":"that's scary. that 'brutish monster' is more intelligent than you...<br /> I guess it would take a good amount of intelligence to perfectly craft a dream to appeal to a person's basic fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:22:44-08:00","id":803318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797883-how-intelligent-is-the-horror?p=803277#post803277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Horror has always greater Intelligence than the Beast. Power = Intelligence + Lair trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Due to their primordial nature, spirits are simpler creatures in rules terms. Instead of the nine Attributes used to define creatures in the physical world, spirits have just three: Power, Finesse and Resistance. <b>This does not mean that all spirits with Power 5 are super genius Olympic weightlifter gymnasts with charismas that dwarf Eva Longoria and Donald Trump.</b> Remember, they are <i>alien</i> creatures. Spirits should be taken on their own terms and mechanics, only compared to one another.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:21:56-08:00","id":803356,"title":"","content":"I think this has gone slightly off what I meant with this thread. I probably put it in a misleading way at the top, but what I meant by intelligent was how self aware a Horror is. Does it think in simple cunning or does it reason, extrapolating into the future? Is a Horror sapient, sentient, both or neither?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T19:13:36-08:00","id":803500,"title":"","content":"Well in so far as they are fragments of the whole both, however there are points to look at from Beasts who have undergone the retreat. The greedy squid (pg 236-39) implies that an unfettered horror does at least have some degree of sapience since it is expressly called out as recalling its creation and therefore occasionally missing opportunities to feed because it wants to know the situation more. Sentience is a question though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}